/*
 * assert-private-implicit-pin.compact — private data may be used in an assert
 * condition without an extra disclose() because the boolean outcome is
 * implicitly disclosed.
 *
 * Official (do not invent APIs):
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/writing
 *   "the use of private data to compute the boolean value of an assert
 *    subexpression is allowed to be implicitly disclosed"
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/guides/security-best-practices
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1487 (test-and-debug samples fail on
 * disclosure and context patterns). Related to language pin ~0.23.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * LOCAL-TRUE. Source only. Not compiled here. Not deployed.
 * This file does not fix the public indexer or node.
